  "location": "2.4 and 2.5",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "cabozantinib: 2.4 and 2.5 give different instructions for one patient",
      "summary": "2.4 reads “180 mg”. 2.5 reads “80 mg”. Example: A patient started at 180 mg (strong CYP3A4 inducer, 2.4) or at 80 mg (hepatic impairment, 2.5) who has an adverse reaction has no resume level in 2.2, which lists only 140, 100 and 60 mg. The text is in this label.",
      "impact": "Potential effect on a prescribing decision: medium. Arxo does not say which instruction is correct and gives no dose."
    }
  },
